the surface duo a dual screen review  by me joanna stern yep this is the 399  surface duo and it's clearly not your  average android smartphone or  tablet it's got not one but two  5.6 inch displays and this 11 megapixel  camera which i'm using to record these  little selfie videos  so for this review i figured the best  thing i could do was take your video  screen  and split it right in half to show you  what the duo does  best oh and yeah you'll see random bugs  just happen on here  opening and closing helps but before i  explain the good and bad of having two  screens  let's take a look at this crazy thing  the duo has four positions  or as microsoft calls them this is a  book posture  posture posture do you remember this  posture i do  there's book mode where the two pop-tart  size screens give you a lot of real  estate  and how i ended up using this thing most  of the time there's single screen mode  where you flip one screen back  there's laptop mode though typing like  this is just  asking for carpal tunnel and tent mode  which is great for watching videos  i really like the hardware it's compact  like a paperback  or a moleskine notebook although many of  us wouldn't really want to put these in  our pockets  i'm calling it there's never been a  better time for a good old  fanny pack anyway great hardware  and for fourteen hundred dollars it  should be but software  not so much over the past two weeks of  testing i encountered  loads of performance issues and bugs no  not the crickets you hear outside my  garage where we've been shooting this  the ones that shouldn't exist on a  product this expensive nothing at all  a few days ago microsoft released a  software update that fixed some of the  issues  but certainly not all especially around  the slow and laggy performance  the company says it will continue to  deliver monthly updates to bring further  refinements to the surface duo  but when the software cooperated here's  where two screens were very useful  s